# alab/removed-paths — upstream paths codex-alab does not carry.
#
# One git pathspec per line, relative to the repository root; a line starting with `#` is a
# comment. alab/sync.sh re-applies every entry after each upstream merge: a conflict inside
# a removed path resolves to the removal, and a file upstream adds under one is dropped.
# Remove upstream content only by adding its path here and `git rm`-ing it in the same
# commit; alab/delta.sh flags an upstream file deleted any other way.

# OpenAI's GitHub automation and repository metadata. As shipped, its CI would run on every
# push to main here, its cron job daily, and Dependabot would open pull requests; the rest is
# what those workflows call (composite actions, CI and release/signing scripts) or GitHub UI
# for OpenAI's org (CODEOWNERS, issue forms, the codex app's config). codex-alab runs no CI:
# alab/check.sh is the gate a sync passes. Upstream's release recipe stays readable with
# `git show upstream/main:.github/<path>`, and alab/watched-paths calls out its changes.
# Nothing ALab owns can live under .github while this entry stands.
.github

